* File balopt.opt of the BYOC scenario.
* All options of base/model/balopt.opt, except that endogenous decommissioning of exogenous capacity is switched off.
* BYOC takes the (net) capacity of the reference run as exogenous. With these options on, the DECOM add-on would
* recalculate GKFX so that it only increases, and 'REVERT' could bring back capacity that the reference run had retired
* (for example fossil plants), which would contradict "no new fossil capacity".
* Endogenous decommissioning of new investments (renewables, storage) keeps the base settings.
* TransInvest is NO in the base options, so no transmission investments are made.

$include '../../base/model/balopt.opt'

$setglobal NO_DECOM_EXO_G
$setglobal LIFETIME_DECOM_EXO_G
$setglobal ECONOMIC_DECOM_EXO_G
$setglobal REVERT_DECOM_EXO_G
